<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pavel Tsitsianov</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1754">1754</a>–<a href="/years/1806">1806</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pavel Tsitsianov was a Russian general of Georgian descent who commanded Russian forces in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a> from 1802. He stormed Ganja in January 1804, killing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/javad-khan">Javad Khan</a>, and forced several khanates to accept Russian protection. In February 1806 he was killed outside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baku">Baku</a> while receiving the city's surrender from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huseyngulu-khan">Huseyngulu Khan</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pavel-tsitsianov.jpg" alt="Pavel Tsitsianov" width="320" height="388" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Salvatore Tonci · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mikhail_Dmitrievich_Tsitsianov.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
